.DS_Store
Conjuguer.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
Conjuguer.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
# Machine-local Claude Code permission grants — not shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

# TelemetryDeck app ID — copy Conjuguer/Secrets.example.xcconfig to
# Conjuguer/Secrets.xcconfig and fill in your app ID. Never commit Secrets.xcconfig.
Conjuguer/Secrets.xcconfig
# ios-build-verify
# .claude/ios-build-verify.config.sh is deliberately NOT ignored: it holds only project
# facts (scheme, bundle ID, launch anchor, the hand-measured 5-tab coordinates), and a
# clone needs it for the documented build path to work.
build/
build.log
docs/screenshots/
# Apple-copyrighted WWDC transcripts, archived locally for reference only (per their headers)
docs/wwdc2026-*.txt
# corpus: tracked = finished JSON exports (corpus/json/), the hand-built parsed
# intermediates (corpus/grokked/ — irreplaceable manual transcription/translation), and
# the build script. Ignored = source PDFs/text (originals/, large + reconstructable) and
# progress notes (working/*.md).
corpus/*
!corpus/json/
!corpus/grokked/
!corpus/working/
corpus/working/*
!corpus/working/build_chanson_examples.py
!corpus/working/build_corpus_index.py
!corpus/working/build_tail_index.py
!corpus/working/build_literature_examples.py
!corpus/working/mine_examples.workflow.js
!corpus/working/build_classical_index.py
!corpus/working/merge_classical.py
!corpus/working/mine_classical.workflow.js
# verb pass (prompts/verb-pass-plan.md): the two Stage 0 reference builders. Their outputs
# (the kaikki dumps, the per-verb reference JSON, conjugations.json, authors.json) stay
# ignored: they are large, and re-running these scripts rebuilds any of them.
!corpus/working/build_wiktionary_reference.py
!corpus/working/build_author_table.py
# Stage 1's six deterministic audits, their shared loader, and the hand-maintained whitelist
# that keeps the unknown-word rule from reporting a century of ordinary English as suspect.
# Their outputs live under corpus/working/verb_pass/ and stay ignored: re-running rebuilds them.
!corpus/working/verb_pass_lib.py
!corpus/working/audit_conjugations.py
!corpus/working/audit_flags.py
!corpus/working/lint_glosses.py
!corpus/working/check_examples.py
!corpus/working/build_candidates.py
!corpus/working/build_verb_pass_shards.py
!corpus/working/gloss_lint_whitelist.txt
# The pilot and Stage 2/3 runner, the pilot scorer, the Stage 2/3 result validator, and the
# Stage 3 skeptic-shard, report and review-page builders. The shard files, the result files, the pilot
# answer key and approvals.json stay ignored under corpus/working/verb_pass/.
!corpus/working/verb_pass.workflow.js
!corpus/working/score_pilot.py
!corpus/working/validate_verb_pass.py
!corpus/working/build_skeptic_shards.py
!corpus/working/build_report.py
!corpus/working/build_review_page.py
# authors_overrides.json is the exception: hand-checked corrections to the Wikidata
# resolution, which nothing regenerates. Re-including one file inside an excluded directory
# takes three lines, because git never descends into a directory it has already excluded.
!corpus/working/wiktionary/
corpus/working/wiktionary/*
!corpus/working/wiktionary/authors_overrides.json

# frequency: tracked = the pipeline scripts, the derived per-verb counts, the hand-maintained
# editorial tier, and GLÀFF's README (its licence asks that it accompany redistribution of
# derived data). Ignored = the two source lexicons (206 MB, re-downloadable per
# frequency/README.md) and the generated report.
frequency/*
!frequency/README.md
!frequency/GLAFF-README.txt
!frequency/*.py
!frequency/verb-counts.json
!frequency/editorial-counts.json
